        ":question/id": "1091cf45-3b7c-52f0-96e3-7f79a1caef3d",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}^{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}} \\frac{6 e^{x}}{2 e^{x} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\ln\\left|u\\right|+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $e^{\\ln 2}=2,\\quad e^{\\ln 3}=3$.\n\n{{answer}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=2 e^{x} + 3$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2 e^{x})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}&\\Longrightarrow u=7\\\\x=\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}&\\Longrightarrow u=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}^{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}} \\frac{6 e^{x}}{2 e^{x} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=3\\left(\\int_{7}^{9} \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\left[\\ln\\left|u\\right|\\right]_{7}^{9}\\right)=3\\left(\\left(\\ln{\\left(9 \\right)}\\right)-\\left(\\ln{\\left(7 \\right)}\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n3\\left(\\ln\\left(9\\right)-\\ln\\left(7\\right)\\right).\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
